  "notes": "A する verb used across many domains. More formal than {取|と}り{除|のぞ}く (to remove), which is the everyday equivalent.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {汚|よご}れを{除去|じょきょ}する (to remove stains/dirt)\n- {障害|しょうがい}を{除去|じょきょ}する (to remove obstacles)\n- {不純物|ふじゅんぶつ}を{除去|じょきょ}する (to remove impurities)\n- {地雷|じらい}{除去|じょきょ} (landmine removal)\n- {除去|じょきょ}{手術|しゅじゅつ} (removal surgery)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {撤去|てっきょ} — removal of structures or installations (demolition, dismantling)\n- {除去|じょきょ} — removal of substances, contaminants, or harmful things",
